1
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,840
Back in the day...

2
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,040
I used to play basketball all the time,

3
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,280
but once I started working, there was...

4
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,920
There was hardly any time left.

5
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,360
Do I still have the moves?

6
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:31,880
Yes, you do.

7
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:58,680
Give me a hand here.

8
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:01,280
I'm going to take my pants off.

9
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:32,280
I'll turn the water on for you.

10
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:33,800
Wait.

11
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:40,920
See?

12
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:42,840
I can't even stand up.

13
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,280
Help me get into the tub.

14
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,520
Also, could you grab me a bathrobe?

15
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,280
What are you so shy about?

16
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,040
We have the same parts.

17
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,400
Could you pull me up?

18
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,200
Did you know...

19
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:06,240
building a body like this...

20
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,240
takes more than just working out?

21
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,240
I didn't.

22
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,320
The most important part is...

23
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,320
right here.

24
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:21,320
Do you know how important the waist is?

25
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,720
You'll understand once you're older.

26
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,160
Have you ever slept with anyone?

27
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:33,760
The noodles are ready.

28
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,079
I'll go get them.

29
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,240
Whoa.

30
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,240
This looks good.

31
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,120
I didn't know you were such a good cook.

32
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,560
I'm only doing this because I hurt your leg.

33
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,560
-Want to have some? -No, thanks.

34
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,000
Oh, leaving already?

35
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,440
I have plans to have dinner with Itt.

36
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,360
Hey, don't tell him I sprained my ankle,

37
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:18,399
or he'll rush over here, okay?

38
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,360
Yeah.

39
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,640
Hey.

40
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,680
Isn't that a bit too formal?

41
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,200
First impressions are everything.

42
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,400
You're dressed way too casually.

43
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,920
You're going to get an earful from my brother.

44
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,760
Isn't this normal?

45
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:40,960
Why?

46
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,960
Worried I won't be around to help you?

47
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,240
You promised you'd help me.

48
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,720
Yeah, I will. Let's go.

49
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,200
Mr. Ing,

50
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,880
the document you just signed was...

51
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,160
a request to increase the budget

52
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,400
by over 20 million.

53
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,840
So?

54
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,280
Look, Secretary Piang.

55
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,920
Don't be such a stress-head.

56
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:17,520
Try to enjoy life, would you?

57
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,200
Just look at me.

58
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,560
Right now, I'm...

59
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:24,080
enjoying the taste of victory before it's mine

60
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,920
because the key to Pattaya...

61
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,120
is about to walk right through that door.

62
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,880
Oh, Mr. Yok...

63
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,120
Exactly.

64
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,720
Understood.

65
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:34,960
In that case,

66
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,400
I'll arrange a desk for Mr. Yok

67
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,159
as close to your office as possible.

68
00:08:38,159 --> 00:08:40,559
I'll also set the AC to the perfect temperature

69
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:41,960
and give him the best view.

70
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,160
If anyone so much as lays a finger

71
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,000
on him,

72
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,280
the fire alarm will go off immediately.

73
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,360
Secretary Piang,

74
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:48,960
could you check

75
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,240
if there are any site visits

76
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,440
on our schedule?

77
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,680
Do you want to see the site,

78
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:55,520
or do you want to see Mr. Yok?

79
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:59,960
The site, obviously. Why would I want to see Yok?

80
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,400
You know, in just...

81
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,280
three, two, one...

82
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,640
What the fuck?

83
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:27,520
That outfit is a total fashion disaster.

84
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,240
What do you think this place is?

85
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,520
A playground?

86
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,640
If you're here for a stroll, do it outside.

87
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:36,880
I think talent should matter more than an outfit.

88
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,000
Secretary Piang,

89
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,080
that's Gen Z for you.

90
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,360
I like it. It shows character.

91
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:46,680
If you have any questions,

92
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,600
ask Piang.

93
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,880
Which department should I put them in?

94
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,400
Which department do you want to intern at?

95
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:55,760
-I'm fine with anything. -Really?

96
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,840
Secretary Piang,

97
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,640
have Auntie Chai...

98
00:09:58,640 --> 00:09:59,520
transferred to another position,

99
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:02,080
and put Itt in as the housekeeper instead.

100
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,560
Fifteen thousand a month, alright?

101
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,880
P'Ing,

102
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,040
I was just kidding.

103
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,160
This is a professional office.

104
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,920
What are you supposed to call me?

105
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,360
Mr. Ing...

106
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,360
Secretary Piang,

107
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,520
put Itt

108
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,200
in Corporate Development.

109
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,520
He'll be right at the front lines

110
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,680
so he can finally get some serious work experience.

111
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:24,160
-Mr. Ing... -As for Yok, stay here in this office.

112
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,720
You'll be my personal assistant.

113
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:29,920
I know exactly what Itt is capable of.

114
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,120
And Yok, you are...

115
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,960
a minor in finance

116
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:36,640
with top-tier grades.

117
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,960
No wonder

118
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,520
you seem so composed.

119
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,160
Having you assist me is for the best.

120
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,480
Secretary Piang is swamped.

121
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,320
You can help her out as well.

122
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:46,880
Understood.

123
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:47,640
Good.

124
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,160
Time for some grooming.

125
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,360
What do you mean?

126
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,040
Having a distinct character is fine,

127
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,160
but from now on,

128
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,600
you represent me.

129
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,240
Come on, let's give you a makeover.

130
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:04,640
I can go buy new clothes

131
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:05,640
with Itt after work.

132
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,400
That won't do.

133
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,160
My time is too valuable.

134
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,400
I can't wait until you're off the clock.

135
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:12,840
What?

136
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:17,200
Do you need a formal letter from the CEO or something?

137
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:18,720
Follow me.

138
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,840
Mr. Itt, please follow me

139
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,520
to the Corporate Development department.

140
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,320
It's the department where...

141
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,080
Hey, Pete.

142
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,480
Hi.

143
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,040
It's been a while, hasn't it?

144
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,080
You finally reached out to me.

145
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,560
I thought you'd forgotten about your old flame.

146
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:00,680
And...

147
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,520
who's this?

148
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,280
This is Yok,

149
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,240
my new assistant.

150
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,520
Oh, my God.

151
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:09,960
He's stunning.

152
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,680
His face is a masterpiece.

153
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Can I touch him?

154
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:19,400
I'm just going to take some measurements.

155
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:21,960
Measure him carefully.

156
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,480
Find a style that I'll actually like.

157
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:26,720
Of course.

158
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,400
As for you...

159
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,000
-Hurry it up. -Based on, uh...

160
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:36,760
You can try something on.

161
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,440
Right this way, please.

162
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:42,160
So handsome.

163
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:44,720
Stunning.

164
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:48,040
Are you ready for the first look?

165
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:48,720
Uh-huh.

166
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:55,440
Ta-da.

167
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,600
Okay.

168
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:10,960
Next one.

169
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,080
So gorgeous.

170
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:20,280
Wow, so handsome.

171
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,920
This one's good. Next.

172
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,800
The third look...

173
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:31,920
Next.

174
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,280
Are you tired?

175
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,480
Ta-da.

176
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,160
This is the final look, Ing.

177
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:39,920
Is that it?

178
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:42,360
I actually wanted him to try on ten outfits.

179
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,960
Never mind. I'll take them all.

180
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,520
I'll be waiting outside.

181
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:48,600
Yes.

182
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,640
Here you go.

183
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:03,760
Everything's ready.

184
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,680
Thanks a lot.

185
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,120
-See you later. -Yeah.

186
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,200
See ya.

187
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,320
What? Are you not coming?

188
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,280
Do you have a thing for the guy with pink hair?

189
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,280
Today was exhausting.

190
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:31,440
You're off the clock. Why are you still here?

191
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,800
How much did everything cost?

192
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:34,920
What?

193
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:36,960
All these clothes.

194
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,680
Oh...

195
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,040
I don't know.

196
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,080
I'll check the total with P'Piang tomorrow

197
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,480
and pay you back right away.

198
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,400
Don't worry about it.

199
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,200
I bought them for you.

200
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,000
Don't worry about the money.

201
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:54,880
Mr. Ing,

202
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:56,800
how could I let you buy all of this for me?

203
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:00,200
Well...

204
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,920
I bought these as a gift for you

205
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,920
so you'll feel more motivated.

206
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,480
Sound good?

207
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,920
Thank you, Mr. Ing.

208
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:10,320
But I'd rather just accept

209
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,800
your kindness.

210
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:17,200
You truly are Minister Pongpaisan's son.

211
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:20,600
Showing respect to both others and yourself.

212
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:21,720
Okay,

213
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:23,560
you win.

214
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,160
I'll put it on my card for now.

215
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:29,960
You can pay me back once you get your salary, okay?

216
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:32,720
Okay.

217
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,160
Money isn't the hard part,

218
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,680
but the work...

219
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,920
is where the real challenge starts.

220
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,000
I'm always ready.

221
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,400
Excuse me.

222
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,280
What's stressing you out?

223
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,760
I need to find a good piece of land

224
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:56,360
at a good price.

225
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,280
Any ideas where?

226
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,040
How about Rayong? It's a major economic hub.

227
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,440
Or Chiang Rai? It connects to both Laos and China.

228
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,760
You're right. Thanks a lot, man.

229
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,280
Stop thinking like that. It's just stupid.

230
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:13,040
So you'll have the strength to keep pushing on.

231
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,960
Hello? I'll send it right away.

232
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:22,840
Sure.

233
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,520
Yok, keep up, or you'll fall behind.

234
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,800
Up here, right?

235
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,240
Yes, put it down here instead.

236
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,360
Yok, take notes.

237
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,720
And over there...

238
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:33,840
I'll go with this plan.

239
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,360
Let's work together to make this project...

240
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,600
Dinner is on me.

241
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,760
You know the rule, no one's going home sober.

242
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:43,920
You bet.

243
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:50,920
Eat up.

244
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,280
You've gotten so thin from working so hard.

245
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:53,840
Take this, P'Phet.

246
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:55,760
Aren't you eating?

247
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:56,840
I'm fine.

248
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,440
To be honest, I'm really glad

249
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,400
I got to meet you today, Mr. Phet.

250
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,440
Me, too. My brother mentions you quite often.

251
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:15,359
Yes, Mr. Ing?

252
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,400
Secretary Piang,

253
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,480
have Yok come see me immediately.

254
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,720
Understood.

255
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,440
Go. Don't waste time,

256
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,840
or he'll blow a fuse again.

257
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,720
He doesn't want me anymore, I see.

258
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:40,320
Mr. Ing, it's payday.

259
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,640
I've already paid for the clothes.

260
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:42,960
Forget about that.

261
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,600
You're coming with me to Damnoen Saduak.

262
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,480
What are we going there for?

263
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,960
I'll tell you on the way.

264
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,440
The proposals submitted to the government official

265
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:57,680
suddenly ran into problems.

266
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:58,800
All the documents

267
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,040
have been sent back for revisions.

268
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,880
The budget, the team,

269
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,200
or the entire plan...

270
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,600
We're waiting on a single document.

271
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,440
I can't afford to mess this up.

272
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,760
Getting a minister and investors together

273
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,440
is no easy feat.

274
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,800
We need to make this deal happen.

275
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,800
Uncle Jeng, please turn the AC up.

276
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:21,720
I'm freezing here.

277
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:22,800
Understood.

278
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:25,800
Do you have a cold?

279
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:27,600
Should we stop and get some medicine?

280
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:29,200
To nip it in the bud, you know.

281
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,160
No need.

282
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,760
It's nothing serious. I'll be fine after a quick nap.

283
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:35,200
By the way, is that data ready?

284
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,400
Let me have a look.

285
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:46,760
I'm screwed.

286
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,600
Yok, can you hold your liquor?

287
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:50,840
Why do you ask?

288
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,480
It's these investors.

289
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,080
They drink like fish

290
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,840
as if there's no tomorrow.

291
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,240
They won't let us leave until we're wasted.

292
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:01,200
Aren't you a heavy drinker yourself?

293
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:03,440
Look at me now.

294
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,600
After two glasses, I'll be down for the count.

295
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,720
Anyway, book a hotel for me today.

296
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:10,200
Sure.

297
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,360
Make sure it's near the place.

298
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,160
Hopefully, I'll be able to crawl back.

299
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,480
Today is extremely important.

300
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:18,520
Whether you drink or not,

301
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,240
you have to keep me in check.

302
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,640
We need to close this deal at any cost.

303
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:24,200
If we can do that,

304
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:25,320
we'll have the chance

305
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,440
to move on to the Pattaya project.

306
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,680
And if we pull it off,

307
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,200
you'll have something to show off to your brother.

308
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,560
This is just how business is.

309
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,840
Having a successful father has its perks,

310
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,080
but once you actually start working,

311
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,320
people act all nice to your face,

312
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:47,840
but behind your back? Jeez...

313
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,960
It's a different story.

314
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,440
They just go through the motions.

315
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,440
I went through the same thing

316
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,040
when I started out in my 20s.

317
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,120
I thought people would respect me.

318
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,520
Not a single one did.

319
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,360
I faced all kinds of problems.

320
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:03,640
Damn it.

321
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,640
It's always just me.

322
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,080
It's cold as hell.

323
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,760
Get some sleep.

324
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,320
I'll wake you up when we get there.

325
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,080
I never would have guessed...

326
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,600
that you're so good at taking care of people.

327
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,800
Wake me up when we arrive.

328
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,400
It's such an honor, Minister.

329
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,840
-Please enjoy yourselves. -We will.

330
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:50,800
Here's to destiny.

331
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:53,080
Thank you, Minister Tawan

332
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:54,840
and Mr. Ing,

333
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,440
for honoring us with your presence today.

334
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,680
-Cheers. -Cheers.

335
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:05,000
This second glass is to sincerity.

336
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:07,920
Whether our partnership succeeds...

337
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,320
depends on how sincere we are with each other.

338
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:12,160
Don't you agree, Mr. Ing?

339
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:17,920
Have some more.

340
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:22,000
Excellent.

341
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,600
The third glass...

342
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:27,560
I can't get out of this one, can I?

343
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,160
Let this glass be...

344
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,040
a testament to my sincerity to everyone.

345
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,520
-Come on. -Let's go, bottoms up.

346
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,920
If you want to do business with me, you need to be bold.

347
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:45,520
Finish this, and I'll sign the contract right away.

348
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:55,480
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

349
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:58,680
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

350
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:01,960
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

351
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,520
Please.

352
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,400
Bottoms up.

353
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,440
Empty it all.

354
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,320
-Go for it. -Do it.

355
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,560
-Drink. -Drink up.

356
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,600
-Whoa. -Whoa.

357
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,400
Mr. Jomthup,

358
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:22,520
I'd like to take this drink on behalf of Mr. Ing.

359
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:23,640
Yok...

360
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,840
You might not understand how we do things here.

361
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:32,440
Exactly.

362
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,080
My father was just talking

363
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,880
about you the other day, Mr. Jomthup.

364
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,280
He enjoyed talking with you about the northern project.

365
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:42,600
Mr. Ravit,

366
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,920
my brother speaks very highly of your vision.

367
00:22:49,560 --> 00:22:50,800
Well then, let's go.

368
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:51,840
Drink up.

369
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:53,120
So, I'd like to raise this glass

370
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,400
as a toast to my respect for all of you.

371
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:57,360
It's our pleasure.

372
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:58,760
-Bottoms up. -Drink.

373
00:22:58,760 --> 00:22:59,520
Drink.

374
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:01,560
Not bad at all.

375
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:05,520
Have another round.

376
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:07,560
-Keep them coming. -Another one.

377
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:10,240
There's still some left. Keep it going.

378
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:11,040
Don't stop.

379
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,800
P'Ing, stay still.

380
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:57,600
Wait.

381
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:01,600
Normally...

382
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,200
aren't you someone

383
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:07,600
who can separate work from personal life?

384
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:11,000
Taking care of my boss is part of my job.

385
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,760
Your boss never taught you anything like this.

386
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:19,120
I'm leaving, then.

387
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:21,800
Hold on.

388
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:24,160
Come here.

389
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:25,920
Come over here.

390
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:33,240
Look...

391
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:35,520
Just a second.

392
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,280
I feel better now.

393
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:50,720
Much better.

394
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,680
You're quite good at taking care of people.

395
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,000
Thanks a lot. I feel a lot better now.

396
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:01,240
Go wash your shirt. It's filthy.

397
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:18,800
Get out of the car.

398
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:31,160
We drove all this way...

399
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:32,600
just to look at a wasteland?

400
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:35,000
This isn't just any ordinary wasteland.

401
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:38,080
It's the fruit of our success from yesterday.

402
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:42,160
Come to think of it...

403
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:45,760
you can really hold your liquor, can't you?

404
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:48,480
I never would've pegged you for that type.

405
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:51,320
To be honest, if I weren't sick,

406
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:54,080
I would've outdrunk those old geezers.

407
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:57,800
So, are you recovered now?

408
00:25:58,320 --> 00:25:59,080
Of course.

409
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:01,120
I'm fit as a fiddle.

410
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,120
If you don't believe me...

411
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:04,440
want to find out?

412
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,520
You're never going to stop, are you?

413
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:10,600
Jeez, why so serious?

414
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,280
Alright.

415
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:13,880
We're here.

416
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:19,800
From now on, this area...

417
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,160
will be where your first building stands.

418
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,280
My first building?

419
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:27,960
Yes.

420
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,560
This will be...

421
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,320
the first building you'll oversee for this project.

422
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,200
What's with the confused look?

423
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,120
No need to get sentimental.

424
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:43,120
You've earned it, Yok.

425
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:50,120
Aren't you going to set foot

426
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:51,880
on the site you'll be managing?

427
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:18,560
From now on,

428
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:22,240
this area is your responsibility.

429
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:35,320
Alright, we should get moving.

430
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:38,400
There's someone important I want to introduce.

431
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:43,880
Why are you just standing there?

432
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,040
Hurry up.

433
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,240
Where are we?

434
00:28:41,080 --> 00:28:41,920
You little rascal.

435
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:46,960
Finally decided to visit your grandpa, huh?

436
00:28:47,920 --> 00:28:50,120
Grandpa, that was a pretty hard pat on the back.

437
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:52,480
Judging by that strength, you'll probably...

438
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,640
live to be at least a hundred and twenty.

439
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:57,040
Why would I want to live that long?

440
00:28:57,600 --> 00:28:58,120
Tell me if you're lonely.

441
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:58,920
I'll find you a wife.

442
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:00,880
Are you serious?

443
00:29:01,200 --> 00:29:02,400
Come on, let's head inside.

444
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:04,720
Oh?

445
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:06,400
Whose kid is this?

446
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:09,320
This is Minister Pongpaisan's son.

447
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:10,360
He's interning with me,

448
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:12,400
so I brought him along to meet you.

449
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:14,840
I see, so it's Pong's grandson.

450
00:29:16,080 --> 00:29:17,560
You certainly have a keen eye for people.

451
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:20,880
Hello, Grandpa. I'm Yok.

452
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:23,960
My, look how much you've grown.

453
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:25,680
When you were just a little thing,

454
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,480
I used to carry you around.

455
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:28,960
Not that you'd remember.

456
00:29:29,200 --> 00:29:31,600
Your grandfather was a stubborn man.

457
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:33,800
He was dead set on giving you a girl's name.

458
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:37,040
He said Yok, or jade, is as precious as diamonds.

459
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:40,360
Everyone tried to stop him, of course,

460
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,720
but no one could change his mind.

461
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:46,200
It's a good thing they couldn't.

462
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,320
I think this piece of jade is...

463
00:29:50,200 --> 00:29:51,400
quite precious indeed.

464
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:55,320
Why are we standing here baking in the sun?

465
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:56,600
Let's go inside.

466
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:58,520
-It's boiling out here. Follow me. -Alright.

467
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:12,800
Know what tree this is?

468
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:16,000
This is called a Pong-pong tree.

469
00:30:16,040 --> 00:30:17,480
Don't ever eat those fruits.

470
00:30:17,520 --> 00:30:18,800
They're lethal.

471
00:30:19,080 --> 00:30:20,360
And this one...

472
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:24,360
When I was a kid, Grandpa tricked me.

473
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,120
He told me it was a banana tree.

474
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,720
I waited for it to bear fruit,

475
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:29,040
but in the end, it didn't.

476
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:31,840
This one...

477
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:33,880
is a Ti plant.

478
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:35,640
Pretty, isn't it?

479
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,400
Not as pretty as me, I guess.

480
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:45,720
Look at this.

481
00:30:46,320 --> 00:30:47,840
I got some pond snails yesterday.

482
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:49,560
I'm going to make a red curry for you.

483
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:53,440
You two, go catch some fish.

484
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,000
I want two big...

485
00:30:56,040 --> 00:30:56,760
nice ones.

486
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,720
Putting us to work again?

487
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:00,560
Yong has the fishing rods ready for you.

488
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:01,640
Same old rule.

489
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,880
If the fish don't weigh at least two kilograms,

490
00:31:04,920 --> 00:31:07,680
you have to do the dishes tonight.

491
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:08,520
Okay.

492
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,400
Just like always, right?

493
00:31:10,760 --> 00:31:11,560
Did you hear that?

494
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:13,280
If you don't want your hands getting all pruney...

495
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:14,920
show me what you've got.

496
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:19,240
Grandpa, he's just putting on an act.

497
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:20,640
He usually knows how to smile.

498
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,440
He just smiles.

499
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:25,400
You got it, Grandpa.

500
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:27,320
Oh, so you can talk.

501
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:41,120
You brought me all this way just to fish?

502
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:43,600
Yok,

503
00:31:44,040 --> 00:31:44,960
let me ask you something.

504
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,440
How were you raised?

505
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:49,520
Why do you have to

506
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:51,480
question everything before doing anything?

507
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,080
We're humans. Just do whatever you want.

508
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:56,760
Want to swim? Swim. Want to fish? Fish.

509
00:31:56,800 --> 00:31:57,680
Eat whatever you want.

510
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,560
Why overthink everything?

511
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:07,600
Come on.

512
00:32:10,040 --> 00:32:11,200
Why are you just standing there?

513
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:12,480
Hurry and bring me some water.

514
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,480
Hurry up.

515
00:32:24,160 --> 00:32:25,240
Why aren't you coming?

516
00:32:25,280 --> 00:32:26,720
Scared of me?

517
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:39,560
Aw, you're scaring me now.

518
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,560
What?

519
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:53,800
How do you like that?

520
00:32:54,320 --> 00:32:55,320
Having fun, huh?

521
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:58,640
P'Ing...

522
00:32:58,960 --> 00:32:59,680
P'Ing.

523
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:11,280
P'Ing, aren't we fishing anymore?

524
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:13,200
Come on, forget about the fish.

525
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:15,000
Let's just swim for now.

526
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:28,600
You little rascal.

527
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:31,800
I told you to fish, but all you did was swim.

528
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:34,720
You've been like this since you were a kid.

529
00:33:35,520 --> 00:33:36,680
You haven't changed either, Grandpa.

530
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:39,040
Still nagging me after all these years.

531
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:40,400
Thailand is just so hot, you know?

532
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,680
Didn't I catch the fish

533
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:43,320
you wanted, anyway?

534
00:33:43,360 --> 00:33:45,360
We got about three or four kilos, right?

535
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:46,880
Yes.

536
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,520
You're quite something, aren't you?

537
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:54,840
Hey, where are you going?

538
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:56,680
I've got the good stuff.

539
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:01,320
He means the liquor.

540
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,440
Have some.

541
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:07,440
Yong, bring the glasses over here.

542
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:13,960
This is Karanda fruit.

543
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:18,560
I grew it and pickled it with my own two hands.

544
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:20,040
Now...

545
00:34:20,080 --> 00:34:20,880
Give me the glasses.

546
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:22,239
Who do you think I take after?

547
00:34:22,520 --> 00:34:23,320
Here.

548
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:31,400
-Make sure you look after your health, too. -Alright.

549
00:34:34,199 --> 00:34:35,280
Here.

550
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:36,639
Three shots.

551
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:41,360
Wait, Grandpa. I'll drink with you.

552
00:34:41,400 --> 00:34:42,520
Yok doesn't drink.

553
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:52,040
That's a very unique flavor.

554
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,800
I thought you said he didn't drink.

555
00:34:57,720 --> 00:34:59,040
Look who's got egg on his face.

556
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,280
Look at you, you little puppy...

557
00:35:02,320 --> 00:35:04,080
Traveling all this way,

558
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:06,200
don't tell me...

559
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:08,120
that you only came here just to visit me.

560
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:11,080
What kind of trouble are you cooking up this time?

561
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:14,560
Come on, you're accusing me already?

562
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:16,200
Are you really my grandpa or what?

563
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,000
Of course I am.

564
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:20,200
Why else would I bother worrying about you?

565
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:25,080
So, what are you really doing here?

566
00:35:29,520 --> 00:35:30,720
Okay, you win.

567
00:35:30,760 --> 00:35:33,440
It's just about the hotel project.

568
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,680
The connections hit a snag,

569
00:35:35,680 --> 00:35:36,560
so things are getting delayed.

570
00:35:36,600 --> 00:35:38,320
I've already sunk all my money into it.

571
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:38,920
Eventually,

572
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:40,560
I'll have to find a new way forward.

573
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,080
You don't need to worry at all.

574
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,880
Looking for a way out is one thing,

575
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:48,400
but don't break the rules.

576
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:49,360
I know.

577
00:35:49,400 --> 00:35:51,840
Don't think having a reputation

578
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:52,760
means you'll get a free pass.

579
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:54,320
Focus on your work

580
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:56,680
and keep yourself on the right track.

581
00:35:56,880 --> 00:35:57,680
Do you hear me?

582
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,360
Understood.

583
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,560
I hear you.

584
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:04,720
Ing here is quite hot-tempered.

585
00:36:05,520 --> 00:36:07,520
Don't let him lead you astray.

586
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:09,280
What, Grandpa?

587
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:12,960
How could someone like me lead him astray?

588
00:36:14,240 --> 00:36:16,040
P'Ing has been taking very good care of me.

589
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:17,800
Well said.

590
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:21,880
Then let's have dinner.

591
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:22,840
Come on.

592
00:36:24,320 --> 00:36:26,240
Yok, keep telling me more

593
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:27,680
about your grandfather.

594
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:29,080
Of course.

595
00:36:30,760 --> 00:36:32,360
Have some curry with pond snails.

596
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:33,600
I made it myself.

597
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:41,920
Honestly,

598
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,760
I feel for you.

599
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:45,360
Here we go again.

600
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,000
When you were a kid,

601
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,720
what you went through...

602
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:52,920
was more than anyone could take.

603
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,880
If your mother were still around...

604
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:56,200
That's enough, Grandpa.

605
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:57,760
That was a long time ago,

606
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,960
and it's all in the past now.

607
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:00,880
You don't have to worry.

608
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:03,560
I'm not gonna jump off a building over this.

609
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,000
That's just how old people are. We talk and talk.

610
00:37:08,720 --> 00:37:09,840
Anyway, you two...

611
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:12,440
must be exhausted by now.

612
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:14,360
I'm getting sleepy.

613
00:37:14,360 --> 00:37:15,200
Not at all.

614
00:37:15,760 --> 00:37:17,440
-What? -I've enjoyed talking with you, Grandpa.

615
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:21,560
This one is quite the smooth talker.

616
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:27,080
If only Ing were half as smooth-talking as you are,

617
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:29,720
I'd be much more at ease.

618
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:31,640
Not at all.

619
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:33,320
I've enjoyed talking with you, Grandpa.

620
00:37:34,720 --> 00:37:35,640
You really are something...

621
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:38,640
Hey, Yong.

622
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:39,760
That's enough, Grandpa.

623
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:40,920
-Go... -Grandpa.

624
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:42,960
I'll have him get the guest room ready for Yok.

625
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:45,400
Yok and I can just share my room.

626
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:47,520
Right? We don't mind a bit of a squeeze.

627
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:51,880
Right, the silent treatment.

628
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:53,200
I'll take that as a yes.

629
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:56,000
Thanks for having me.

630
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,560
Take good care of Yok, alright?

631
00:38:03,720 --> 00:38:04,320
I will.

632
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:12,120
Sorry about this.

633
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:16,560
My grandpa is all about that low-carbon lifestyle,

634
00:38:17,120 --> 00:38:20,000
so there's no AC. Just this old-school fan.

635
00:38:20,640 --> 00:38:22,160
You can handle it, right?

636
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,840
It's fine. It's not that hot anyway.

637
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:41,880
I'm going to hit the shower.

638
00:38:43,520 --> 00:38:44,320
Don't you dare peek.

639
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:16,440
It's your turn now.

640
00:39:22,920 --> 00:39:23,520
Yok...

641
00:39:26,400 --> 00:39:27,000
Yok,

642
00:39:27,360 --> 00:39:28,000
wake up.

643
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:32,720
Go take a shower.

644
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:35,080
No...

645
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,720
You have to.

646
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:38,960
How can you go to bed without showering first?

647
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:40,600
Go shower.

648
00:39:41,520 --> 00:39:43,760
Go take a shower.

649
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:48,480
Go.

650
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:54,360
Your towel is over here.

651
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:04,320
He ruined everything.

652
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:13,720
Oh...

653
00:40:15,120 --> 00:40:18,560
I spilled some water all over the blanket.

654
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:20,800
We'll have to share this one.

655
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:24,400
Hurry up and turn off the lights.

656
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,520
Get to bed.

657
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:56,880
Hey.

658
00:40:59,240 --> 00:41:01,080
Aren't you hot in long sleeves?

659
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:03,400
I'm not.

660
00:41:06,720 --> 00:41:08,520
You'll be too hot to sleep in a bit. Come here.

661
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:10,560
-Let me help you take them off. -I'm fine.

662
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:28,320
What? I was just trying to tuck you in.

663
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:34,520
Suit yourself.

664
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:36,240
If you don't want the blanket, fine.

665
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:39,440
Don't come crying to me if you get sick.

666
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:41,840
Earlier today,

667
00:41:41,880 --> 00:41:43,200
you didn't seem to care if I got sick.

668
00:41:44,440 --> 00:41:46,720
Why are you holding such a grudge?

669
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:06,840
Sorry, I'm a side sleeper.

670
00:42:22,400 --> 00:42:24,440
-What are you doing? -I'm just trying to cover you up.

671
00:42:25,800 --> 00:42:26,920
Wait, where are you going?

672
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:28,600
I'm just trying to tuck you in.

673
00:42:28,600 --> 00:42:29,720
It's nothing.

674
00:42:29,720 --> 00:42:31,600
Come here. I told you to cover up.

675
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:38,440
That hurts.

676
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:53,200
Wait, where are you going?

677
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:59,160
Come visit again when you're free.

678
00:42:59,200 --> 00:43:00,280
Grandpa, I'm not leaving soon.

679
00:43:00,320 --> 00:43:01,200
Who was talking to you?

680
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:01,960
Grandpa...

681
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:03,720
Just who is your actual grandson here?

682
00:43:04,120 --> 00:43:04,680
Hey.

683
00:43:05,280 --> 00:43:06,200
Want to try dating each other?

684
00:43:07,160 --> 00:43:08,600
Whether I like women or not,

685
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,000
there's no way we could be together.

686
00:43:12,560 --> 00:43:14,280
I've endured this for long enough.
